 689:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****   * @brief Receive an amount of data in DMA mode till either the expected number
 690:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****   *        of data is received or an IDLE event occurs.
 691:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****   * @note  Reception is initiated by this function call. Further progress of reception is achieved 
 692:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****   *        to DMA services, transferring automatically received data elements in user reception buf
 693:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****   *        calling registered callbacks at half/end of reception. UART IDLE events are also used to
 694:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****   *        reception phase as ended. In all cases, callback execution will indicate number of recei
 695:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****   * @note  When the UART parity is enabled (PCE = 1), the received data contain
 696:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****   *        the parity bit (MSB position).
 697:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****   * @note  When UART parity is not enabled (PCE = 0), and Word Length is configured to 9 bits (M1-M
 698:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****   *        the received data is handled as a set of uint16_t. In this case, Size must indicate the 
 699:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****   *        of uint16_t available through pData.
 700:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****   * @note  When UART parity is not enabled (PCE = 0), and Word Length is configured to 9 bits (M1-M
 701:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****   *        address of user data buffer for storing data to be received, should be aligned on a half
 702:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****   *        (16 bits) (as received data will be handled by DMA from halfword frontier). Depending on
 703:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****   *        use of specific alignment compilation directives or pragmas might be required
 704:Drivers/STM32F0xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f0xx_hal_uart_ex.c ****   *        to ensure proper alignment for pData.
